{"id": "3bda0484-896a-4744-841a-f49a46471a0c", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm recalling that AnalyzeDocument, being a synchronous Textract API, doesn't use IAM role assumption like the async StartDocumentAnalysis does—the caller's own credentials are what need S3 access, not the service role. That's likely the source of the AccessDenied error even with a properly configured Textract service role.

I'm not fully certain whether Textract itself needs bucket policy permissions as a service principal, or whether it's the caller's IAM permissions that matter for synchronous calls - this is a specific enough AWS detail that I should verify against documentation rather than rely on my recollection.

"}]}

